---
// Faq.astro - Linear / Vercel Minimal Border-Bottom Accordion
---

<section id="faq" class="w-full scroll-mt-20 text-left">
  <!-- Section Header -->
  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white mb-1.5">
      Frequently Asked Questions
    </h2>
    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 font-normal">
      Technical verification, privacy guarantees, and local architecture.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Accordion List with Clean Border-Bottom Dividers (No Bulky Backgrounds) -->
  <div class="border-t border-white/10 divide-y divide-white/10">
    
    <!-- FAQ 1 -->
    <details class="group py-4 transition-all">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-white text-sm sm:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between select-none hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors">
        <span>How does CleanPhoto destroy EXIF metadata without a server?</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 flex-shrink-0 ml-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        CleanPhoto operates 100% inside your browser's JavaScript engine. It loads your image onto an offscreen <code class="text-slate-200 bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/[0.08] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">HTML5 Canvas</code> at full native dimensions and re-encodes pure pixel data into a fresh Blob. Because canvas rasterization only copies pixel color channels (RGBA), metadata blocks like EXIF APP1, IPTC, XMP, and GPS coordinates are physically dropped.
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 2 -->
    <details class="group py-4 transition-all">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-white text-sm sm:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between select-none hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors">
        <span>How can I independently verify zero network traffic?</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 flex-shrink-0 ml-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        You can independently prove this at any time:
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong>Airplane Mode:</strong> Load the web app, disconnect your internet connection, and drop any photo. CleanPhoto continues to parse, sanitize, and export files completely offline.</li>
          <li><strong>DevTools Network Tab:</strong> Open DevTools (<kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-white/[0.04] text-[10px] font-mono border border-white/[0.08]">F12</kbd>), switch to the Network tab, and process images. You will see 0 outbound HTTP or WebSocket requests.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 3 -->
    <details class="group py-4 transition-all">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-white text-sm sm:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between select-none hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors">
        <span>Will my photo lose dimensions, resolution, or sharpness?</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 flex-shrink-0 ml-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        No. The canvas width and height match <code class="text-slate-200 bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/[0.08] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">naturalWidth</code> and <code class="text-slate-200 bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/[0.08] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">naturalHeight</code> pixel-for-pixel with high-precision smoothing enabled. By default, pristine 95% quality is applied for JPEG and 100% lossless compression for PNG.
      </div>
    </details>

    <!-- FAQ 4 -->
    <details class="group py-4 transition-all">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-white text-sm sm:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between select-none hover:text-slate-200 transition-colors">
        <span>Which image formats are supported?</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-slate-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-200 flex-shrink-0 ml-3" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19.5 8.25l-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5" />
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <div class="pt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        CleanPhoto supports all modern web image formats: <strong>JPEG / JPG, PNG, and WebP</strong>. You can choose to preserve the original format or cross-convert during export.
      </div>
    </details>

  </div>
</section>
